WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.256
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:03.526 --> 00:05.590
Pilseung!

3
00:05.590 --> 00:09.551
To Sergeant Kim Sang Hun! I am currently at the latrine,

4
00:09.551 --> 00:13.389
and I am reporting to ask if I may inquire about the possibility of

5
00:13.389 --> 00:17.250
requesting permission to commence urination!

6
00:19.793 --> 00:21.688
You crazy bastard! That's a spot-on impression!

7
00:21.688 --> 00:23.566
I actually wanted to join the Marines...

8
00:23.566 --> 00:24.793
You, a Marine?

9
00:24.793 --> 00:27.010
Just get your act together here first.

10
00:39.501 --> 00:40.893
Hey...

11
00:41.667 --> 00:42.835
Are you here to have fun?

12
00:42.835 --> 00:45.129
Kim Sang Hun. Have you lost your mind too?

13
00:45.129 --> 00:46.297
I'm sorry.

14
00:46.297 --> 00:49.133
You've lost your minds, mocking another branch like that...

15
00:49.133 --> 00:52.261
You think I delayed my discharge to stick around for this nonsense?

16
00:52.261 --> 00:53.985
I'm sorry...

17
00:55.167 --> 00:56.723
I apologize.

18
00:56.723 --> 00:58.850
It's their first big exercise with another branch...

19
00:58.850 --> 01:00.269
That was out of line.

20
01:00.269 --> 01:01.979
So you're the top dog?

21
01:01.979 --> 01:03.549
The top dog?

22
01:04.189 --> 01:06.316
What do you Army guys call it... the old-timer?

23
01:06.316 --> 01:08.459
Your most senior soldier.

24
01:08.459 --> 01:10.404
Yes, that's me.

25
01:10.404 --> 01:13.365
I heard you say you delayed your discharge?

26
01:13.365 --> 01:14.908
Yes, well...

27
01:17.119 --> 01:21.498
This exercise is hardly worth delaying your discharge for...

28
01:21.498 --> 01:24.943
But I guess it's a big deal for you Army guys?

29
01:27.042 --> 01:28.046
Excuse me?

30
01:28.046 --> 01:29.626
Never mind.

31
01:29.626 --> 01:31.425
Anyway,

32
01:31.425 --> 01:34.426
that's admirable, Sergeant Kang.

33
01:37.597 --> 01:38.599
What was that...

34
01:38.599 --> 01:40.142
Did that jerk just look down on me?

35
01:40.142 --> 01:41.226
Yeah...

36
01:41.226 --> 01:43.927
So rude, with a smile on his face.

37
01:44.646 --> 01:46.440
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, I'm sorry...

38
01:46.440 --> 01:48.150
This is all my fault...

39
01:48.150 --> 01:49.776
Get your act together.

40
01:49.776 --> 01:51.111
Stop embarrassing us.

41
01:51.111 --> 01:53.071
- Yes, I'm sorry. - Understood.

42
01:53.071 --> 01:55.234
I ought to kick you.

43
01:56.033 --> 01:57.292
I'm sorry.

44
01:57.292 --> 01:58.952
Forget it.

45
01:58.952 --> 02:00.928
- Let's just keep quiet. - Yes.

46
02:03.000 --> 02:06.293
[Operations headquarters]

47
02:06.293 --> 02:07.911
First Lieutenant Oh.

48
02:08.587 --> 02:10.797
Sorry I didn't recognize you on the mountain earlier.

49
02:10.797 --> 02:14.301
You had so much camo paint on, I thought you were an enlisted man.

50
02:14.301 --> 02:15.385
No need to apologize.

51
02:15.385 --> 02:17.554
I was in the middle of an operation and failed to give my rank and name.

52
02:17.554 --> 02:20.029
I was the one being rude.

53
02:20.029 --> 02:21.016
Wait.

54
02:21.016 --> 02:23.393
You're First Lieutenant Oh too, aren't you?

55
02:23.393 --> 02:25.386
So is Seok Jin here.

56
02:26.396 --> 02:28.607
"Oh" means five, so two First Lieutenant "Oh"s...

57
02:28.607 --> 02:30.394
make First Lieutenant Ten?

58
02:35.709 --> 02:37.125
It's not funny. Stop laughing.

59
02:37.125 --> 02:38.408
I'm sorry.

60
02:38.408 --> 02:39.834
Anyway, it's raining.

61
02:39.834 --> 02:42.079
When's the exercise controller getting here?

62
02:42.079 --> 02:44.373
If we get someone strict, we're in for a headache.

63
02:44.373 --> 02:47.668
We Marines don't care who the controller is.

64
02:47.668 --> 02:52.029
Marines answer only to other Marines.

65
02:53.417 --> 02:57.386
These Marines certainly have some spirit, don't they?

66
02:57.386 --> 03:01.894
[Hoguk exercise controller: Sergeant Major Jang Tae San]

67
03:03.292 --> 03:06.853
Looks like all our North Korean troops are here.

68
03:06.853 --> 03:08.417
Instructor Jang Tae San?

69
03:08.417 --> 03:10.065
Captain Cho Baek Ho.

70
03:10.065 --> 03:11.608
It's been a while since the advanced officer course, hasn't it?

71
03:11.608 --> 03:13.527
[A mandatory military training program for captains] Yes.

72
03:13.527 --> 03:17.072
And there's our spirited Staff Sergeant Ma Tae Ho.

73
03:17.072 --> 03:18.579
Pil...

74
03:18.579 --> 03:20.250
Pilseung!

75
03:20.250 --> 03:22.628
Pilseung, you rascal.

76
03:22.628 --> 03:26.322
- Wait, you've made sergeant first class? - Yes, I have.

77
03:27.416 --> 03:30.417
But you haven't made major yet, Captain Cho?

78
03:34.631 --> 03:36.758
- Oh, you've been selected for promotion? - No.

79
03:36.758 --> 03:39.125
This is my last chance to be considered.

80
03:39.125 --> 03:41.388
When you came to the advanced officer course as a captain,

81
03:41.388 --> 03:43.862
I was still a master sergeant.

82
03:44.474 --> 03:47.018
- It'll work out, Captain Cho. - Yes.

83
03:47.018 --> 03:51.931
If officers like you don't belong in the military, who does?

84
03:52.858 --> 03:55.777
Let's do well in this exercise and get you promoted.

85
03:55.777 --> 03:57.070
Thank you.

86
03:57.070 --> 03:59.656
All right, enough small talk.

87
03:59.656 --> 04:03.201
Let's begin the situation briefing.

88
04:03.201 --> 04:08.039
We're a light infantry brigade under the North Korean Army's Storm Corps.

89
04:08.039 --> 04:11.792
We've crossed the 38th parallel and are advancing south.

90
04:11.792 --> 04:16.548
Our forces are bogged down in the forward sector,

91
04:16.548 --> 04:18.675
but if the defensive line ahead collapses,

92
04:18.675 --> 04:22.345
the enemy's main force will pour through here.

93
04:22.345 --> 04:26.850
Now, suppose South Korean special forces fast-rope onto Hill 300,

94
04:26.850 --> 04:32.230
here in our sector, to cut off our supply route.

95
04:32.230 --> 04:34.191
[Rapid rope descent from a hovering helicopter] How do we stop them?

96
04:34.191 --> 04:36.818
Let's hear your ideas.

97
04:36.818 --> 04:41.156
How about having our main Army force set up a blocking position below?

98
04:41.156 --> 04:43.867
Defending that position would play to our strengths.

99
04:43.867 --> 04:47.621
Our Marines are far more mobile than the Army.

100
04:47.621 --> 04:50.540
Why not use that advantage to sweep uphill to Hill 300,

101
04:50.540 --> 04:53.098
finding and destroying the enemy as we go?

102
04:53.098 --> 04:54.419
Wouldn't that be better?

103
04:54.419 --> 04:56.463
They're coming downhill.

104
04:56.463 --> 04:59.424
Wouldn't attacking uphill put you at a disadvantage?

105
04:59.424 --> 05:00.884
Marines fight in any conditions.

106
05:00.884 --> 05:03.042
We don't blame the terrain.

107
05:03.042 --> 05:04.429
Oh, really?

108
05:04.429 --> 05:06.280
Impressive, you Marines.

109
05:06.949 --> 05:08.100
Good.

110
05:08.100 --> 05:10.185
You both have a point.

111
05:10.185 --> 05:12.103
But...

112
05:12.103 --> 05:15.334
You, the Army staff sergeant. You keep looking around for cues.

113
05:15.334 --> 05:16.983
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

114
05:16.983 --> 05:18.652
What do you think?

115
05:18.652 --> 05:22.823
Well, if the enemy's coming down from above,

116
05:22.823 --> 05:25.784
and our Army troops are holding the bottom,

117
05:25.784 --> 05:29.412
the Marines, with all their stamina, could hunker down halfway up,

118
05:29.412 --> 05:30.834
while us grunts...

119
05:30.834 --> 05:33.708
Oh! I'm sorry.

120
05:33.708 --> 05:38.380
Our Army troops could wait below.

121
05:38.380 --> 05:41.143
Then we could sandwich the enemy between us.

122
05:41.792 --> 05:43.735
I like it.

123
05:45.429 --> 05:46.888
You were a conscript first, weren't you?

124
05:46.888 --> 05:48.932
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

125
05:48.932 --> 05:50.292
- Yes, I was. - I thought so.

126
05:50.292 --> 05:54.000
You've still got that barracks vocabulary.

127
05:54.000 --> 05:55.042
Thank you.

128
05:55.042 --> 05:59.067
Anyway, remember that you're all on the same team

129
05:59.067 --> 06:01.667
when you plan your tactics.

130
06:01.667 --> 06:05.031
We'll have a rehearsal tomorrow before the main exercise.

131
06:05.031 --> 06:07.667
My men will play the opposing side.

132
06:07.667 --> 06:08.618
Yes.

133
06:08.618 --> 06:11.667
I'll leave you to it.

134
06:11.667 --> 06:13.430
Captain Cho,

135
06:14.041 --> 06:15.696
it'll work out.

136
06:18.459 --> 06:20.042
Yes.

137
06:20.042 --> 06:22.339
I've talked your ears off.

138
06:23.883 --> 06:27.369
Why is it raining so much?

139
06:48.667 --> 06:50.907
I'm so hungry.

140
06:51.494 --> 06:53.248
Excuse me, Marine.

141
06:54.331 --> 06:55.415
Excuse me.

142
06:55.415 --> 06:57.208
Yes?

143
06:57.208 --> 07:00.125
I'm sorry about earlier today.

144
07:00.125 --> 07:03.965
I wasn't thinking. I just kept eating.

145
07:03.965 --> 07:05.592
It's been bothering me.

146
07:05.592 --> 07:08.000
I think I got you in trouble with your seniors.

147
07:08.000 --> 07:10.222
I'm really sorry.

148
07:10.222 --> 07:11.473
It's okay.

149
07:11.473 --> 07:13.250
You must be hungry.

150
07:13.250 --> 07:14.267
Here, have this.

151
07:14.267 --> 07:17.209
I'd stashed it away to eat by myself tonight.

152
07:17.209 --> 07:18.438
But I'll make an exception for you.

153
07:18.438 --> 07:21.374
Marines don't get hungry.

154
07:23.792 --> 07:26.529
Come on. I can hear your stomach growling. Just have it.

155
07:26.529 --> 07:29.032
- Here. - I was told...

156
07:29.032 --> 07:30.659
only sloppy, undisciplined Marines

157
07:30.659 --> 07:32.626
- eat on duty. - Nobody's watching.

158
07:32.626 --> 07:33.787
Go ahead. Okay?

159
07:33.787 --> 07:36.475
I need to poop, so I have to go.

160
07:37.083 --> 07:39.334
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

161
07:39.334 --> 07:41.176
Thank you.

162
07:42.837 --> 07:45.674
Looks like we're in the same boat.

163
07:45.674 --> 07:47.301
Have that. It'll keep you going.

164
07:47.301 --> 07:49.302
Actually, just eat it now. I'll keep watch.

165
07:49.302 --> 07:50.679
Go on. Eat it.

166
07:50.679 --> 07:52.332
Thank you.

167
08:05.709 --> 08:07.195
What's going on, Assey?

168
08:07.195 --> 08:08.822
Private Choi Uk.

169
08:08.822 --> 08:10.417
Are you allowed to chat while on duty?

170
08:10.417 --> 08:12.325
Pilseung!

171
08:12.325 --> 08:13.584
No incidents to report.

172
08:13.584 --> 08:15.829
What was that rustling?

173
08:15.829 --> 08:17.919
And why are you talking funny?

174
08:20.375 --> 08:21.460
Oh, man.

175
08:21.460 --> 08:23.670
So this is where I dropped my Choco Pie.

176
08:23.670 --> 08:25.459
Come on.

177
08:25.459 --> 08:27.390
I've been looking for this.

178
08:29.551 --> 08:31.000
Remember, Assey.

179
08:31.000 --> 08:33.847
A Marine stays in formation, even in death. Understood?

180
08:33.847 --> 08:35.223
Yes!

181
08:35.223 --> 08:37.508
Stay focused on your watch.

182
08:40.103 --> 08:43.255
Pilseung!

183
08:55.326 --> 08:59.209
[EP09. Marines]

184
08:59.209 --> 09:02.957
Now this feels like a real exercise.

185
09:02.957 --> 09:06.792
[Army-Marine opposing force camp: rehearsal] Park Min Seok, don't touch that sensor.

186
09:06.792 --> 09:09.792
If you bump it and it registers you as dead, you're out.

187
09:09.792 --> 09:11.259
Really?

188
09:11.259 --> 09:12.719
By the way, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

189
09:12.719 --> 09:17.265
When we fire, does a blank go off and this thing shoot a laser?

190
09:17.265 --> 09:18.850
Right.

191
09:18.850 --> 09:21.709
During company tactical drills, we make our own gunfire sounds.

192
09:21.709 --> 09:22.834
Yes, that's right.

193
09:22.834 --> 09:24.397
Bang, bang, bang!

194
09:24.397 --> 09:27.400
But with this, every time a blank goes off,

195
09:27.400 --> 09:32.280
the data shows up live on the GPS display on the controller's tablet.

196
09:32.280 --> 09:35.241
Who shot whom, who's been hit, who's dead.

197
09:35.241 --> 09:38.459
There's no point insisting, "I wasn't hit."

198
09:38.459 --> 09:40.705
Check each other's gear. Make sure it's on right.

199
09:40.705 --> 09:42.663
- Understood. - Understood.

200
09:45.918 --> 09:48.755
Understood. You and Kang Mu Jeok can cover this flank,

201
09:48.755 --> 09:50.340
Assistant Platoon Leader.

202
09:50.340 --> 09:51.925
- How does that sound? - Yes, understood.

203
09:51.925 --> 09:53.384
Hey, he said not to touch that.

204
09:53.384 --> 09:56.555
- Do it right. - Understood.

205
09:56.555 --> 09:57.680
Got it?

206
09:57.680 --> 09:59.224
Yes.

207
09:59.224 --> 10:00.642
Cheol Yong.

208
10:00.642 --> 10:02.769
We're getting all the kills today.

209
10:02.769 --> 10:05.230
Don't let those Army grunts have a single one. Got it?

210
10:05.230 --> 10:07.107
Corporal Park Cheol Yong.

211
10:07.107 --> 10:10.626
I'll show them why the Marines never lose.

212
10:10.626 --> 10:12.028
That's the spirit.

213
10:12.028 --> 10:13.321
All right, everyone, listen up.

214
10:13.321 --> 10:15.261
- Listen up! - Listen up!

215
10:15.924 --> 10:18.284
Today's a rehearsal for the main exercise.

216
10:18.284 --> 10:20.959
But you know we're treating it like real combat, right?

217
10:20.959 --> 10:22.205
- Yes! - Ah!

218
10:22.205 --> 10:24.207
Don't say "ah."

219
10:24.207 --> 10:26.423
Il Gu. Come here a second.

220
10:28.125 --> 10:30.172
- Hold this for a second. - Yes.

221
10:30.172 --> 10:31.876
Here's the situation.

222
10:31.876 --> 10:34.968
We're a light infantry brigade under the North Korean Army's Storm Corps.

223
10:34.968 --> 10:37.846
We're defending our rear sector.

224
10:37.846 --> 10:40.056
According to the latest intelligence,

225
10:40.056 --> 10:45.019
South Korean special forces will fast-rope onto Hill 300.

226
10:45.019 --> 10:49.691
Their objective is to break through us and cut off our supply route.

227
10:49.691 --> 10:51.818
Our plan is to surround and destroy them.

228
10:51.818 --> 10:53.278
- Marines. - Ah!

229
10:53.278 --> 10:54.654
I told you to stop saying "ah."

230
10:54.654 --> 10:57.907
You'll set up an ambush halfway up, on Hill 200.

231
10:57.907 --> 11:01.286
The Army will establish a blocking position on Hill 100.

232
11:01.286 --> 11:03.830
Once they enter our zone,

233
11:03.830 --> 11:06.416
we'll crush them from above and below at the same time.

234
11:06.416 --> 11:07.959
- Understood? - Yes, understood.

235
11:07.959 --> 11:10.044
- All right, Second Company. - Second Company!

236
11:10.044 --> 11:11.546
Move to Hill 100, on the double!

237
11:11.546 --> 11:13.339
- Move out! - Come on, let's move.

238
11:13.339 --> 11:15.884
Il Gu, you really came through.

239
11:15.884 --> 11:17.343
You were born to be a soldier.

240
11:17.343 --> 11:18.880
Thank you.

241
11:19.709 --> 11:21.055
Good luck, First Lieutenant Oh.

242
11:21.055 --> 11:22.056
Yes, sir.

243
11:22.056 --> 11:24.667
Not you. First Lieutenant Oh from the Marines.

244
11:24.667 --> 11:25.852
Be careful.

245
11:25.852 --> 11:27.145
You too, Captain Cho.

246
11:27.145 --> 11:28.771
Pilseung!

247
11:28.771 --> 11:30.514
Chungseong!

248
11:33.526 --> 11:35.195
Looking good. I've got high hopes.

249
11:35.195 --> 11:36.957
Stay safe out there, sir.

250
11:38.115 --> 11:39.130
Go ahead.

251
11:39.130 --> 11:40.632
This looks promising.

252
11:43.459 --> 11:45.148
Here.

253
11:47.167 --> 11:49.101
- Let's move out too. - Yes, sir.

254
11:49.101 --> 11:51.167
[On Hill 100] Take your time digging.

255
11:51.167 --> 11:53.125
Only seven more to go.

256
11:53.125 --> 11:54.464
Come on, let's get this done.

257
11:54.464 --> 11:56.459
- Understood. - Understood.

258
11:56.459 --> 11:58.885
Who taught you to dig like that, you knucklehead?

259
11:58.885 --> 12:00.667
- Are you talking to me? - Who else would I be talking to?

260
12:00.667 --> 12:02.972
- Didn't anyone teach you how to dig? - I'm sorry.

261
12:02.972 --> 12:04.641
Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

262
12:04.641 --> 12:08.436
I heard we're wearing North Korean uniforms for the actual exercise tomorrow.

263
12:08.436 --> 12:10.000
Yeah, I heard that too.

264
12:10.000 --> 12:11.709
We're dressing up just like North Korean soldiers, right?

265
12:11.709 --> 12:13.325
Yes.

266
12:15.360 --> 12:18.780
Wouldn't Sergeant Kang Chan Seok look good in one?

267
12:18.780 --> 12:20.626
How so?

268
12:20.626 --> 12:24.375
Doesn't he look like North Korea's defense minister?

269
12:24.375 --> 12:25.915
A North Korean.

270
12:27.080 --> 12:29.709
Want me to show you some deadly force?

271
12:29.709 --> 12:31.626
You heard that?

272
12:31.626 --> 12:33.285
I'm sorry.

273
12:34.545 --> 12:36.340
- Sergeant Kang Chan Seok. - Yes.

274
12:36.340 --> 12:40.083
There's something I've really wanted to ask you.

275
12:40.083 --> 12:42.346
- Go ahead. - Do you really have no regrets

276
12:42.346 --> 12:44.305
about postponing your discharge?

277
12:44.918 --> 12:45.974
Regrets?

278
12:45.974 --> 12:47.642
You bet I do.

279
12:47.642 --> 12:50.312
I keep wondering what I'm even doing here.

280
12:50.312 --> 12:53.564
Then why did you postpone it?

281
12:53.564 --> 12:54.565
Well,

282
12:54.565 --> 12:57.921
I couldn't sleep easy at home knowing you guys were out here suffering.

283
12:59.250 --> 13:00.613
I'd rather tough it out with you,

284
13:00.613 --> 13:03.352
get it over with, and go home with a clear conscience.

285
13:03.950 --> 13:04.951
That's loyalty.

286
13:04.951 --> 13:06.537
Quit asking questions and keep digging, punk.

287
13:06.537 --> 13:07.787
Yes, comrade.

288
13:07.787 --> 13:09.959
You little...

289
13:09.959 --> 13:12.834
There he goes, acting cool again.

290
13:12.834 --> 13:14.876
What about you, Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam?

291
13:14.876 --> 13:15.918
Any regrets?

292
13:15.918 --> 13:17.880
I regret ever getting mixed up with this guy.

293
13:17.880 --> 13:20.258
What did I think I'd get out of it?

294
13:20.258 --> 13:23.584
- Oh, the company commander's here. - Chungseong! Love you!

295
13:23.584 --> 13:25.278
Just kidding.

296
13:27.266 --> 13:29.500
Look, sir. They're slacking off.

297
13:29.500 --> 13:30.519
Fooled you again.

298
13:30.519 --> 13:32.292
That really isn't funny.

299
13:32.292 --> 13:34.209
Get to work, you punks. We need these holes dug fast.

300
13:34.209 --> 13:35.274
Hey, Moon Bit Na Ri.

301
13:35.274 --> 13:37.568
Get a move on, comrade.

302
13:37.568 --> 13:38.651
Sure thing, comrade.

303
13:38.651 --> 13:40.362
That's no way to talk to a superior, idiot.

304
13:40.362 --> 13:42.292
I'm sorry. But isn't that how North Koreans talk?

305
13:42.292 --> 13:44.533
- Just keep digging. - Yes.

306
13:44.533 --> 13:47.843
[On Hill 200]

307
13:50.542 --> 13:52.582
Hwarang, Hwarang, this is Blue Dragon, Blue Dragon.

308
13:52.582 --> 13:55.984
Blue Dragon has reached Hill 200. Over.

309
14:09.016 --> 14:11.959
Look at this terrain.

310
14:11.959 --> 14:16.042
We'll break our shovels before we can dig in.

311
14:16.042 --> 14:18.918
What do you think, Assistant Platoon Leader?

312
14:18.918 --> 14:21.083
Should we change the plan?

313
14:21.083 --> 14:23.696
This is the plan we agreed on.

314
14:23.696 --> 14:26.181
I'm not sure we can change it.

315
14:30.584 --> 14:32.872
Let's change it.

316
14:32.872 --> 14:36.542
If we can't dig in here, we'll head up and attack first.

317
14:36.542 --> 14:37.585
Understood.

318
14:37.585 --> 14:41.471
That's the Marine spirit. Keep at it until you succeed.

319
14:42.131 --> 14:43.508
Everyone, listen up.

320
14:43.508 --> 14:44.675
- Listen up. - Listen up.

321
14:44.675 --> 14:46.803
Change of plans.

322
14:46.803 --> 14:50.139
We're heading straight up to Hill 300.

323
14:50.139 --> 14:52.225
We'll tear the enemy apart in the air

324
14:52.225 --> 14:54.185
before they can set foot on the ground.

325
14:54.185 --> 14:55.978
- Understood? - Yes!

326
14:55.978 --> 14:58.751
All hands, charge up to Hill 300.

327
14:58.751 --> 15:00.388
- Yes! - Yes!

328
15:06.792 --> 15:10.417
[On Hill 100]

329
15:10.417 --> 15:13.496
Blue Dragon, Blue Dragon. This is Hwarang. Over.

330
15:13.496 --> 15:14.664
This is Blue Dragon. Over.

331
15:14.664 --> 15:16.250
Are you in position for the ambush? Over.

332
15:16.250 --> 15:18.042
This terrain is unsuitable for an ambush.

333
15:18.042 --> 15:20.128
We're changing tactics. Over.

334
15:20.128 --> 15:21.716
What are you talking about?

335
15:24.465 --> 15:27.083
Blue Dragon is moving to Hill 300.

336
15:27.083 --> 15:29.220
- What's he doing? - We'll strike first

337
15:29.220 --> 15:30.638
as the enemy helicopters descend.

338
15:30.638 --> 15:33.667
Hwarang, move your blocking line uphill. Over.

339
15:33.667 --> 15:35.726
We've already set up our positions on Hill 100.

340
15:35.726 --> 15:37.061
What are you talking about?

341
15:37.061 --> 15:38.559
Stick to the plan.

342
15:39.147 --> 15:40.959
Hey. Oh Kang Cheol.

343
15:40.959 --> 15:42.733
Oh Kang Cheol.

344
15:42.733 --> 15:45.528
That lunatic. Unbelievable.

345
15:45.528 --> 15:47.927
Having some trouble?

346
15:48.959 --> 15:51.429
Let's see.

347
15:52.368 --> 15:53.751
Captain Cho.

348
15:54.620 --> 15:56.834
The Marines aren't following the plan.

349
15:56.834 --> 15:59.900
Charge!

350
16:07.292 --> 16:10.678
Already at odds, are you?

351
16:10.678 --> 16:13.414
Damn those Marines.

352
16:15.125 --> 16:16.741
This is entertaining.

353
16:18.542 --> 16:20.606
- Second Company. - Second Company.

354
16:20.606 --> 16:22.733
We're moving our blocking line uphill. Grab all your gear and follow me.

355
16:22.733 --> 16:24.567
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

356
16:24.567 --> 16:26.027
- Come on. Let's move. - Let's move.

357
16:26.027 --> 16:27.334
Hey, come on. Let's move.

358
16:27.334 --> 16:29.751
- Yes. - This is driving me nuts.

359
16:29.751 --> 16:34.480
[On Hill 250]

360
16:43.542 --> 16:44.670
Huh?

361
16:44.670 --> 16:47.491
Company Commander, look over there.

362
16:49.417 --> 16:51.219
Those lunatics. Damn it.

363
16:51.219 --> 16:53.221
Everyone, use cover and stay concealed. Charge!

364
16:53.221 --> 16:54.305
- Charge! - Charge!

365
16:54.305 --> 16:56.389
Those idiots.

366
17:08.402 --> 17:10.626
Hang in there.

367
17:10.626 --> 17:13.242
Almost there.

368
17:13.242 --> 17:14.242
Company Commander.

369
17:14.242 --> 17:16.764
[On Hill 300]

370
17:31.542 --> 17:32.677
What was that?

371
17:32.677 --> 17:34.417
What? Did I get hit?

372
17:34.417 --> 17:35.751
Where are they?

373
17:35.751 --> 17:37.125
Take cover!

374
17:37.125 --> 17:39.291
- Take cover. - Take cover.

375
17:41.083 --> 17:42.780
What?

376
17:44.709 --> 17:46.065
I think I've been hit.

377
17:46.065 --> 17:47.650
What?

378
17:47.650 --> 17:49.250
Oh, come on.

379
17:49.250 --> 17:50.334
I've been hit.

380
17:50.334 --> 17:51.571
I think I've been hit.

381
17:51.571 --> 17:53.115
- Wait, you're dead? - Yes, sir.

382
17:53.115 --> 17:55.129
- You're dead? - I'm dead, sir.

383
17:55.792 --> 17:57.792
What? You're all dead?

384
17:57.792 --> 17:59.394
Yes, we are all dead.

385
18:00.414 --> 18:02.425
Circle around.

386
18:07.042 --> 18:09.542
What are you doing? Get it together.

387
18:09.542 --> 18:12.014
- I'm sorry. - We'll do better.

388
18:13.969 --> 18:17.054
Marines never die.

389
18:17.054 --> 18:23.853
They just become legends.

390
18:24.645 --> 18:26.229
I'm sorry.

391
18:27.000 --> 18:28.899
Hey, Oh Kang Cheol.

392
18:28.899 --> 18:30.610
Where's Oh Kang Cheol?

393
18:30.610 --> 18:31.736
Oh Kang Cheol.

394
18:31.736 --> 18:33.279
First Lieutenant Oh Kang Cheol.

395
18:33.279 --> 18:34.834
What are you doing?

396
18:34.834 --> 18:36.074
Is this a joke?

397
18:36.074 --> 18:37.615
I'm sorry.

398
18:39.410 --> 18:41.236
What is this?

399
18:44.540 --> 18:46.450
Exercise over.

400
18:49.920 --> 18:51.881
Unbelievable. What a mess.

401
18:51.881 --> 18:54.804
You're far worse than I expected.

402
18:55.509 --> 18:59.508
Do I need to replace the opposing force?

403
19:00.307 --> 19:01.682
- Captain Cho? - Yes.

404
19:01.682 --> 19:03.299
Let's talk.

405
19:04.603 --> 19:06.346
Oh Kang Cheol, come with me.

406
19:18.250 --> 19:20.334
Unbelievable.

407
19:20.334 --> 19:22.167
You Army clowns.

408
19:22.167 --> 19:25.161
You're so slow, you're just dead weight.

409
19:26.082 --> 19:29.368
You should've gotten here sooner to back us up.

410
19:37.083 --> 19:39.345
Hey, you jerk.

411
19:39.345 --> 19:43.809
Who ignored orders and charged ahead on their own,

412
19:43.809 --> 19:45.876
leaving a gap in our lines?

413
19:45.876 --> 19:47.353
You think I...

414
19:47.353 --> 19:49.918
You think I delayed my discharge

415
19:49.918 --> 19:51.982
and joined this exercise just to hear this nonsense?

416
19:51.982 --> 19:53.792
Sergeant Kang.

417
19:53.792 --> 19:56.320
Now you've crossed the line.

418
19:56.320 --> 19:58.042
How dare you lay a hand on a Marine?

419
19:58.042 --> 19:58.989
Marines? Big deal.

420
19:58.989 --> 20:01.301
- You think you're something special? - What?

421
20:01.301 --> 20:02.542
You Army punks.

422
20:02.542 --> 20:04.469
What did you say, you jerk?

423
20:08.834 --> 20:10.876
Let go. Stay out of this, you jerk.

424
20:10.876 --> 20:13.212
- Hey, you idiots. - Please stop.

425
20:13.212 --> 20:15.914
- Marines! - Are you kidding me?

426
20:17.675 --> 20:19.468
You're a nobody.

427
20:19.468 --> 20:21.083
Say that again. Say it again.

428
20:21.083 --> 20:22.221
Hey, you idiots.

429
20:22.221 --> 20:24.339
- Do you want to die? - Hey.

430
20:27.834 --> 20:30.104
You're on the same side. What are you doing?

431
20:30.104 --> 20:31.789
Are you out of your minds?

432
20:34.375 --> 20:36.435
You idiots.

433
20:43.042 --> 20:45.819
Everyone.

434
20:50.626 --> 20:52.922
Freeze.

435
20:55.379 --> 20:57.757
Everyone, attention.

436
20:57.757 --> 20:59.341
Pilseung.

437
20:59.341 --> 21:01.209
Oh, First Sergeant. You're here.

438
21:01.209 --> 21:04.088
Pilseung.

439
21:05.307 --> 21:06.704
Chungseong.

440
21:08.185 --> 21:09.685
What brings you here?

441
21:09.685 --> 21:10.853
Hello.

442
21:10.853 --> 21:12.856
I'm Master Sergeant Lee Jung Gu

443
21:12.856 --> 21:15.108
from the Marine Amphibious Raiding Battalion.

444
21:15.108 --> 21:16.692
I came to deliver food supplies

445
21:16.692 --> 21:19.686
and saw my men behaving disrespectfully.

446
21:20.321 --> 21:23.562
May I have a word with them?

447
21:24.658 --> 21:25.953
Go ahead.

448
21:25.953 --> 21:27.416
Thank you.

449
21:30.542 --> 21:33.125
What are you, a bunch of street thugs?

450
21:33.125 --> 21:35.753
Since when did the Marines

451
21:35.753 --> 21:40.522
become an undisciplined mob that ignores the chain of command?

452
21:42.092 --> 21:44.470
Eyes that can stare down the sun.

453
21:44.470 --> 21:47.056
A voice so loud your guts could burst.

454
21:47.056 --> 21:50.667
Don't you know that's the bare minimum for a Marine?

455
21:51.644 --> 21:55.064
But look at you now.

456
21:55.064 --> 21:57.441
You've lost all your discipline.

457
21:57.441 --> 21:59.735
Stop looking around.

458
21:59.735 --> 22:02.292
I can hear your eyes moving from here.

459
22:02.292 --> 22:05.449
- I'll do better. - We'll do better.

460
22:05.449 --> 22:09.245
General Shin Hyeon Jun, our first commandant,

461
22:09.245 --> 22:14.333
said your life should weigh no more than a feather on the battlefield.

462
22:14.333 --> 22:18.629
Yet you can't let go of your petty pride,

463
22:18.629 --> 22:21.674
so you cause trouble during training?

464
22:21.674 --> 22:25.094
Get it together before I rip those red name tags off your chests.

465
22:25.094 --> 22:26.167
- Understood? - Yes!

466
22:26.167 --> 22:28.556
Is that all the volume you can muster? Understood?

467
22:28.556 --> 22:30.331
- Yes! - Yes!

468
22:31.792 --> 22:35.121
Oh, man. What a commanding presence.

469
22:38.607 --> 22:40.317
Thank you for allowing me to address them.

470
22:40.317 --> 22:41.777
Of course.

471
22:41.777 --> 22:44.962
You're absolutely right, Master Sergeant Lee.

472
22:45.656 --> 22:49.451
Troops who disobey their commander die before the enemy does.

473
22:49.451 --> 22:51.495
- Understood? - Yes, sir.

474
22:51.495 --> 22:53.497
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

475
22:53.497 --> 22:55.184
Marine Park Cheol Yong.

476
23:01.547 --> 23:04.508
I just recovered your personal effects.

477
23:04.508 --> 23:06.058
Understood?

478
23:11.140 --> 23:14.184
We were all killed in that engagement.

479
23:14.184 --> 23:18.439
So we'll practice casualty evacuation on the way down.

480
23:18.439 --> 23:22.234
Army troops can carry Marines, or vice versa.

481
23:22.234 --> 23:24.320
You can switch on the way down.

482
23:24.320 --> 23:29.742
But one complaint, and you go straight back to the starting point. Understood?

483
23:29.742 --> 23:30.910
- Yes, sir. - Yes.

484
23:30.910 --> 23:31.619
Understood?

485
23:31.619 --> 23:33.245
- Yes, sir. - Yes.

486
23:33.245 --> 23:34.246
Form up for evacuation.

487
23:34.246 --> 23:36.090
- Form up. - Form up.

488
23:38.792 --> 23:39.834
I'll do better.

489
23:39.834 --> 23:41.128
Are you okay?

490
23:41.128 --> 23:42.900
I'm sorry.

491
23:42.900 --> 23:44.751
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

492
23:44.751 --> 23:46.425
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

493
23:46.425 --> 23:47.908
Let's go.

494
23:48.584 --> 23:50.077
I'm sorry.

495
23:56.959 --> 23:59.542
Why is the company commander making us do this?

496
23:59.542 --> 24:00.856
I'm sorry.

497
24:00.856 --> 24:03.361
- Watch your step. - Yes, thank you.

498
24:04.500 --> 24:06.363
- Hey, Byeong Ho. Are you okay? - I'm fine.

499
24:06.363 --> 24:07.459
Thanks a lot.

500
24:07.459 --> 24:09.667
Slow down, Marine.

501
24:09.667 --> 24:11.867
My guts are about to spill out.

502
24:11.867 --> 24:14.329
Marines don't fall.

503
24:14.329 --> 24:16.705
Are you from Jeolla, by any chance?

504
24:16.705 --> 24:20.209
Yeah. Hwasun, just south of Gwangju.

505
24:20.209 --> 24:22.294
Oh? I'm from Hwasun too.

506
24:22.294 --> 24:24.505
What? Hwasun?

507
24:24.505 --> 24:26.006
I'm from Hwasun Township.

508
24:26.006 --> 24:27.549
What?

509
24:27.549 --> 24:30.209
Me too. Hwasun Township.

510
24:30.209 --> 24:32.680
Can't believe I'd run into someone from back home here.

511
24:32.680 --> 24:35.265
The Tigers have been driving you nuts lately, huh?

512
24:35.265 --> 24:39.021
They brought in Manager Sun, and they're still in fifth place.

513
24:39.021 --> 24:40.521
That says it all.

514
24:40.521 --> 24:43.150
They should banish the whole team to Hampyeong.

515
24:43.150 --> 24:45.500
They should just disband the team.

516
24:45.500 --> 24:47.319
Your legs look a little shaky.

517
24:47.319 --> 24:48.542
Want me to take a turn?

518
24:48.542 --> 24:50.781
You don't weigh a thing, so could you just shut your mouth,

519
24:50.781 --> 24:52.413
Mr. Marine Boy?

520
24:59.124 --> 25:01.959
Wait! Cramp.

521
25:01.959 --> 25:03.536
A cramp.

522
25:04.296 --> 25:05.918
Straighten your leg.

523
25:05.918 --> 25:07.292
It's the other foot.

524
25:07.292 --> 25:09.994
Oh, come on. You're unbelievable.

525
25:17.601 --> 25:19.735
Take ten.

526
25:19.735 --> 25:21.311
- Take ten. - Take ten.

527
25:21.311 --> 25:22.938
Marines, take ten too.

528
25:22.938 --> 25:24.950
Take ten.

529
25:25.649 --> 25:28.259
Where did Bit Na Ri go this time?

530
25:29.278 --> 25:30.487
Bit Na Ri, hurry up.

531
25:30.487 --> 25:32.425
Hurry up.

532
25:33.824 --> 25:36.130
Are you okay, Marine?

533
25:36.959 --> 25:39.834
- I'm fine. - You don't look okay.

534
25:39.834 --> 25:42.624
Let's switch when we get over there.

535
25:42.624 --> 25:44.253
I'd appreciate that.

536
25:44.253 --> 25:45.971
Assey.

537
25:46.966 --> 25:49.757
- What's wrong? - But I think I'd better keep going.

538
25:49.757 --> 25:51.675
I'll take over for you in a bit.

539
25:51.675 --> 25:53.022
Yes!

540
25:53.679 --> 25:55.407
Here, eat this.

541
25:56.667 --> 25:58.851
It's My Gummy.

542
25:58.851 --> 26:00.143
Thank you.

543
26:00.143 --> 26:01.500
Hang in there. We're almost there.

544
26:01.500 --> 26:02.500
Thank you.

545
26:02.500 --> 26:03.879
Want another?

546
26:05.230 --> 26:06.106
One for me too.

547
26:06.106 --> 26:08.358
By the way, did you wash your hands?

548
26:08.358 --> 26:10.153
- I washed them this morning. - Oh, this morning.

549
26:10.153 --> 26:11.717
I see.

550
26:12.667 --> 26:14.918
How old are you?

551
26:14.918 --> 26:16.658
I was born in 1990.

552
26:16.658 --> 26:18.976
I'm older, so I'll drop the formalities, okay?

553
26:20.247 --> 26:23.248
You look older, so go right ahead.

554
26:23.248 --> 26:26.036
What? You nut.

555
26:28.589 --> 26:30.547
So, Sergeant Kang, when were you supposed to get out?

556
26:30.547 --> 26:32.466
Today, but I put it off.

557
26:32.466 --> 26:33.884
What about you?

558
26:33.884 --> 26:36.285
Next month.

559
26:37.764 --> 26:39.640
We're short-timers. We shouldn't even risk a falling leaf.

560
26:39.640 --> 26:41.310
What are we doing putting ourselves through this?

561
26:41.310 --> 26:43.310
Close to getting out?

562
26:43.310 --> 26:46.262
I'm a civilian, man.

563
26:47.022 --> 26:50.360
By that logic, once I get back and go on my final leave,

564
26:50.360 --> 26:52.544
I'm practically a civilian too.

565
26:53.237 --> 26:55.364
My back hurts.

566
26:55.364 --> 26:58.075
Your turn to carry me.

567
26:58.075 --> 27:00.329
You nearly broke a civilian's ribs back there.

568
27:00.329 --> 27:02.243
Sure thing.

569
27:03.205 --> 27:05.324
Hop on, bro.

570
27:06.750 --> 27:08.957
How did you carry me down this slope?

571
27:09.578 --> 27:10.584
You're so heavy.

572
27:10.584 --> 27:12.132
Could you pick up the pace a little?

573
27:12.132 --> 27:14.343
How am I supposed to go faster?

574
27:14.343 --> 27:16.666
Let's pick up the pace.

575
27:21.640 --> 27:22.766
We can do it.

576
27:22.766 --> 27:24.565
We got this.

577
27:26.230 --> 27:28.148
- Now you give me a piggyback. - Got it.

578
27:28.148 --> 27:29.972
Let me carry you.

579
27:31.735 --> 27:33.687
I'm sorry.

580
27:35.614 --> 27:38.200
- Snacks at the PX are on you when we get down. - Yes.

581
27:38.200 --> 27:40.265
Quit fooling around.

582
27:41.076 --> 27:43.370
I've got everything.

583
27:43.370 --> 27:45.499
I'm okay.

584
27:45.499 --> 27:47.666
How are you with the Second Company Commander?

585
27:47.666 --> 27:50.959
You mean Captain Cho Baek Ho?

586
27:50.959 --> 27:54.918
I hear this is his last shot at promotion.

587
27:54.918 --> 27:57.419
Yes, that's my understanding.

588
27:58.510 --> 28:01.120
What do you think?

589
28:04.393 --> 28:06.393
What do you mean, sir?

590
28:06.393 --> 28:08.730
Is keeping a soldier like Captain Cho Baek Ho

591
28:08.730 --> 28:13.892
good for the Army or bad for it?

592
28:15.959 --> 28:18.017
Well...

593
28:19.375 --> 28:21.628
I think...

594
28:25.037 --> 28:27.121
he's a good soldier.

595
28:33.250 --> 28:35.401
Pick up the pace!

596
28:43.334 --> 28:45.250
This is awesome.

597
28:45.250 --> 28:47.809
Write down these words of wisdom from me.

598
28:47.809 --> 28:50.334
Even without Big Farm or canned tuna,

599
28:50.334 --> 28:52.981
Matdasi will get you through any exercise.

600
28:52.981 --> 28:54.728
That's right.

601
28:57.042 --> 28:58.459
- Come on, really mix it! - Yes.

602
28:58.459 --> 29:00.239
- Hey, mix it well. - Understood.

603
29:00.239 --> 29:01.865
Bit Na Ri's really good at mixing this.

604
29:01.865 --> 29:04.284
Moon Mix-a-Lot.

605
29:04.284 --> 29:06.955
I got good at this helping out in the kitchen.

606
29:06.955 --> 29:08.292
Don't get cocky.

607
29:08.292 --> 29:09.458
Yes.

608
29:09.458 --> 29:12.753
Hey, offer the Marines some, too.

609
29:12.753 --> 29:15.253
Would you like to try some with us?

610
29:15.253 --> 29:17.566
We don't eat that stuff.

611
29:18.884 --> 29:21.142
This guy's still trying to act tough.

612
29:21.142 --> 29:22.554
Kang Mu Jeok?

613
29:22.554 --> 29:25.057
Looks like your men are waiting for your okay.

614
29:25.057 --> 29:27.042
What are you talking about?

615
29:27.042 --> 29:29.546
You make it sound like I bully them...

616
29:32.980 --> 29:35.190
I'll have some first, then.

617
29:35.190 --> 29:36.500
Go ahead and help yourselves.

618
29:36.500 --> 29:37.903
Sergeant Kang Mu Jeok.

619
29:37.903 --> 29:40.042
- Pilseung! - What is it?

620
29:40.042 --> 29:42.375
We may have gotten a little closer during training,

621
29:42.375 --> 29:44.209
- Now, let me give this a try. - but doesn't it look bad

622
29:44.209 --> 29:45.327
to mooch off the Army?

623
29:45.327 --> 29:47.162
You startled me.

624
29:47.162 --> 29:48.912
- Hey. - Corporal Park Cheol Yong.

625
29:48.912 --> 29:50.415
Right, Cheol Yong.

626
29:50.415 --> 29:52.708
If your superior poops in a helmet, what is that?

627
29:52.708 --> 29:55.043
- An operation. - Then what do you think I'm doing now?

628
29:55.043 --> 29:56.839
- An operation. - Exactly.

629
29:56.839 --> 29:59.174
I don't see this as mooching.

630
29:59.174 --> 30:00.882
A good Marine knows how other branches eat.

631
30:00.882 --> 30:03.509
- Got it? - I'll do better.

632
30:13.334 --> 30:14.563
What?

633
30:14.563 --> 30:17.459
This tastes incredible!

634
30:17.459 --> 30:18.459
Everyone, charge!

635
30:18.459 --> 30:20.235
- Charge! - Charge!

636
30:20.235 --> 30:21.278
Move over.

637
30:21.278 --> 30:22.321
What?

638
30:22.321 --> 30:24.417
Take your time.

639
30:24.417 --> 30:26.074
There's plenty.

640
30:26.074 --> 30:28.579
- Hey, you're kicking up dust! - Slow down.

641
30:28.579 --> 30:30.078
- Hey, hurry up and try it. - Thank you.

642
30:30.078 --> 30:32.459
- Private Choi Uk. - Private First Class Jeong Woo Cheol.

643
30:32.459 --> 30:35.042
Is this red stuff gochujang?

644
30:35.042 --> 30:36.417
It's Matdasi.

645
30:36.417 --> 30:38.879
Wait, don't you guys have Matdasi?

646
30:38.879 --> 30:40.757
We don't have that in the Marines.

647
30:40.757 --> 30:42.341
I'll give you some to take back.

648
30:42.341 --> 30:43.425
Thank you.

649
30:43.425 --> 30:45.083
We're from the same neck of the woods.

650
30:45.083 --> 30:46.375
- Please, dig in. - Eat up.

651
30:46.375 --> 30:48.055
- You mixed this really well. - Thank you.

652
30:48.055 --> 30:49.250
Have as much as you like.

653
30:49.250 --> 30:51.221
This is really good.

654
30:56.607 --> 30:58.607
So this is Matdasi.

655
30:58.607 --> 31:02.051
Hey, Bit Na Ri, we need another batch.

656
31:02.903 --> 31:04.446
Hold on!

657
31:04.446 --> 31:07.115
A Marine can't just take without giving back.

658
31:07.115 --> 31:09.034
- Hey, Cheol Yong. - I'll go get it.

659
31:09.034 --> 31:10.417
- Corporal Seong Gi Jung. - Hey, Woo Cheol,

660
31:10.417 --> 31:11.870
- you two go get it. - Private Choi Uk.

661
31:11.870 --> 31:13.792
- Go on, hurry up. - What is it?

662
31:13.792 --> 31:15.207
Hurry.

663
31:17.000 --> 31:19.913
This is semi-dried squid from Guryongpo.

664
31:20.714 --> 31:22.756
We brought it to snack on while waiting in ambush.

665
31:22.756 --> 31:25.969
Wouldn't this taste even better if we tore some up and mixed it in?

666
31:25.969 --> 31:28.058
I'll mix it right in.

667
31:33.083 --> 31:34.434
You can do it!

668
31:34.434 --> 31:36.292
You can do it!

669
31:36.292 --> 31:37.626
That's good.

670
31:37.626 --> 31:39.042
Cheol Yong, come here.

671
31:39.042 --> 31:40.565
- Thank you. - Do you like squid?

672
31:40.565 --> 31:42.484
I do.

673
31:42.484 --> 31:44.227
It's also part of your training.

674
31:45.113 --> 31:47.221
It tastes like squid and pork bulgogi.

675
31:48.281 --> 31:51.410
Adding that Guryongpo squid was genius.

676
31:51.410 --> 31:54.204
Spicy-sweet Matdasi with chewy squid.

677
31:54.204 --> 31:55.288
It's so good!

678
31:55.288 --> 31:57.459
We need to make this a regular thing.

679
31:57.459 --> 31:59.198
Delicious!

680
32:04.459 --> 32:08.837
11, 12, 13.

681
32:15.684 --> 32:16.685
Take a breath.

682
32:16.685 --> 32:18.186
Bring them up together.

683
32:18.186 --> 32:19.598
Thrust.

684
32:19.598 --> 32:20.605
- Strike. - Strike.

685
32:20.605 --> 32:22.125
- You block with one hand. - Okay.

686
32:22.125 --> 32:23.751
- One hand. - I understand perfectly.

687
32:23.751 --> 32:26.319
Thrust again, then strike.

688
32:26.319 --> 32:28.334
- Strike. - Strike.

689
32:28.334 --> 32:30.292
- You block with one hand. - Oh, I see.

690
32:30.292 --> 32:31.918
Am I that far off?

691
32:31.918 --> 32:33.785
You're doing well, Sergeant.

692
32:33.785 --> 32:35.626
- You've got this! - All right, here we go.

693
32:35.626 --> 32:37.542
- Thrust, strike, thrust, strike. - Thrust, strike, thrust, strike.

694
32:37.542 --> 32:38.751
- Okay. - One.

695
32:38.751 --> 32:39.751
- Two. - Keep it up!

696
32:39.751 --> 32:40.792
- Two. - Two.

697
32:40.792 --> 32:41.793
Gummy, gummy, yum, yum.

698
32:41.793 --> 32:43.294
- Three. - Three.

699
32:43.294 --> 32:44.709
Oh, that's sweet. Four.

700
32:44.709 --> 32:46.792
- Four. - Four...

701
32:46.792 --> 32:48.008
Grape flavor.

702
32:48.008 --> 32:49.157
- Five. - Five.

703
32:49.157 --> 32:50.385
Delicious. Six.

704
32:50.385 --> 32:51.667
Six.

705
32:51.667 --> 32:53.054
See you next time. Seven.

706
32:53.054 --> 32:54.139
- Seven. - Seven.

707
32:54.139 --> 32:55.167
Chewy, chewy. Eight.

708
32:55.167 --> 32:57.875
- What are you talking about? - Eight.

709
33:00.979 --> 33:04.209
Anyone who falls behind does 100 push-ups!

710
33:04.209 --> 33:05.275
Understood?

711
33:05.275 --> 33:06.918
- Yes! - Yes!

712
33:06.918 --> 33:08.292
All right, good work, everyone.

713
33:08.292 --> 33:10.257
Well done.

714
33:14.709 --> 33:16.125
- One, two. - One, two.

715
33:16.125 --> 33:17.746
- One, two, three. - One, two, three.

716
33:17.746 --> 33:19.664
- One, two. - One, two.

717
33:19.664 --> 33:21.834
- One, two. - One, two.

718
33:21.834 --> 33:23.901
Open wide.

719
33:26.125 --> 33:27.872
Are you all right?

720
33:30.209 --> 33:31.526
Ah!

721
33:35.430 --> 33:37.584
That's refreshing!

722
33:37.584 --> 33:39.500
That's the Marine spirit!

723
33:39.500 --> 33:41.957
Ah! Thank you, Platoon Leader.

724
33:42.584 --> 33:44.559
What a character.

725
33:46.733 --> 33:47.842
Really?

726
33:47.842 --> 33:49.694
Then I'm older than you.

727
33:49.694 --> 33:52.864
[Ten hours before the operation begins] Not that I'll drop the formalities.

728
33:52.864 --> 33:54.908
How's that, Chan Seok?

729
33:54.908 --> 33:56.584
You're the best, Mu Jeok.

730
33:56.584 --> 33:57.702
That looks good on you.

731
33:57.702 --> 33:59.074
Once you're out of the Marines, come join the Army.

732
33:59.074 --> 34:00.751
Once a Marine, always a Marine.

733
34:00.751 --> 34:01.873
You're adorable.

734
34:01.873 --> 34:03.542
Right here, you bring it down hard.

735
34:03.542 --> 34:04.667
Like this, bam!

736
34:04.667 --> 34:07.334
M-o-o-n-l-i-g-h-t.

737
34:07.334 --> 34:09.000
Moonlight.

738
34:09.000 --> 34:10.542
Hey, listen up.

739
34:10.542 --> 34:12.427
- Listen up! - Listen up!

740
34:12.427 --> 34:17.055
Special Forces has probably already figured out all the tactics we used today.

741
34:17.055 --> 34:19.724
I think we'll have to change our approach completely

742
34:19.724 --> 34:21.726
to stand a chance in tomorrow's main exercise.

743
34:21.726 --> 34:23.334
Now listen carefully.

744
34:23.334 --> 34:25.021
Chungseong.

745
34:25.021 --> 34:27.756
Oh, sorry.

746
34:29.778 --> 34:31.278
Were you having a strategy meeting?

747
34:31.278 --> 34:32.946
Yes. What brings you here?

748
34:32.946 --> 34:35.784
I thought you might be hungry, so I brought you some snacks.

749
34:35.784 --> 34:38.992
You could've let us know. We could've picked them up.

750
34:39.577 --> 34:43.915
Why'd everyone go quiet when I walked in?

751
34:43.915 --> 34:48.736
Worried I'll listen in and tell our Special Forces guys?

752
34:52.009 --> 34:53.542
There's no need for that.

753
34:53.542 --> 34:55.552
Let's be honest.

754
34:55.552 --> 34:58.346
Our Special Forces guys are career soldiers who do nothing but train.

755
34:58.346 --> 35:01.516
Of course they're stronger than regular infantry.

756
35:01.516 --> 35:02.809
- Yes. - Right?

757
35:02.809 --> 35:07.272
Besides, the opposing force doesn't have to follow a set playbook.

758
35:07.272 --> 35:12.611
If you can't beat them head-on, shake things up and catch them off guard.

759
35:12.611 --> 35:16.114
Win by any means necessary.

760
35:16.114 --> 35:19.701
That's the opposing force's job.

761
35:19.701 --> 35:22.287
- Thank you for the advice. - Oh, don't mention it.

762
35:22.287 --> 35:24.875
I've talked long enough.

763
35:24.875 --> 35:26.876
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

764
35:26.876 --> 35:27.792
Eat up.

765
35:27.792 --> 35:30.596
- Take care, sir. - Take care, sir.

766
35:31.882 --> 35:34.709
You heard him, right? He's a sly old fox.

767
35:34.709 --> 35:35.884
Watch what you say.

768
35:35.884 --> 35:36.876
- Yes, sir. - Yes!

769
35:36.876 --> 35:38.626
Hey, no shouting.

770
35:38.626 --> 35:40.180
Come to think of it,

771
35:40.180 --> 35:43.266
he already knew our whole plan yesterday, didn't he?

772
35:43.266 --> 35:44.603
- That's right. - That's right.

773
35:44.603 --> 35:46.584
Thinking about it gives me chills.

774
35:46.584 --> 35:49.522
Then we don't have to worry about what the exercise controller thinks.

775
35:49.522 --> 35:53.234
Like he just said, let's use any means necessary.

776
35:53.234 --> 35:57.783
Anyone have a good plan to catch Special Forces off guard?

777
35:57.783 --> 35:59.171
You go.

778
36:01.659 --> 36:03.918
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Yes.

779
36:03.918 --> 36:06.081
I have a brilliant plan.

780
36:06.081 --> 36:07.794
What is it?

781
36:08.500 --> 36:10.960
The plan is to steal Sergeant Major Jang Tae San's uniform,

782
36:10.960 --> 36:14.005
put it on, and stroll into enemy territory as the exercise controller.

783
36:14.005 --> 36:17.292
Then shoot them all dead while their guard's down.

784
36:17.292 --> 36:18.510
What do you think?

785
36:18.510 --> 36:20.345
"Oh, hey, I'm Jang Tae San."

786
36:20.345 --> 36:22.250
You really think that dumb idea would work?

787
36:22.250 --> 36:23.667
Isn't it a good idea?

788
36:23.667 --> 36:25.709
That was creative.

789
36:25.709 --> 36:29.938
I think we need unconventional tactics like Min Seok's.

790
36:29.938 --> 36:30.939
Thank you.

791
36:30.939 --> 36:33.650
And we've got the Marines with us.

792
36:33.650 --> 36:35.860
- We can pull off anything, right? - Yes!

793
36:35.860 --> 36:37.667
I told you, no shouting.

794
36:37.667 --> 36:39.197
Gather round.

795
36:39.834 --> 36:43.847
Let's shake things up.

796
37:08.636 --> 37:12.167
[Hoguk exercise: D-day]

797
37:12.167 --> 37:13.542
This is Exercise Control.

798
37:13.542 --> 37:14.703
Attention all units,

799
37:14.703 --> 37:16.985
including exercise controllers and the opposing force.

800
37:16.985 --> 37:20.000
The main exercise begins now.

801
37:20.000 --> 37:22.250
All personnel, deploy to your assigned training areas

802
37:22.250 --> 37:24.617
immediately and begin operations.

803
37:24.617 --> 37:27.000
- Out. - Loud and clear.

804
37:27.000 --> 37:30.000
Second Company, let's wipe them out!

805
37:30.000 --> 37:32.310
[On Hill 250]

806
37:52.834 --> 37:54.063
Comrade Company Commander,

807
37:54.063 --> 37:57.584
five Special Forces troops from the main unit are coming down Hill 250.

808
37:57.584 --> 37:58.675
Over.

809
37:58.675 --> 37:59.694
Right.

810
37:59.694 --> 38:03.292
But Da Hye, you don't have to talk like a North Korean.

811
38:03.292 --> 38:04.936
Understood, comrade.

812
38:06.620 --> 38:08.019
I'm sorry.

813
38:23.718 --> 38:26.667
[On Hill 200]

814
38:26.667 --> 38:27.680
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu?

815
38:27.680 --> 38:30.225
When the Special Forces see this empty shell of a position,

816
38:30.225 --> 38:31.976
they'll think it's a trap and go around, right?

817
38:31.976 --> 38:34.479
Zhuge Liang used the Empty Fort Strategy.

818
38:34.479 --> 38:37.815
He opened the gates and scared off Sima Yi's army.

819
38:37.815 --> 38:39.736
Have you read Romance of the Three Kingdoms?

820
38:39.736 --> 38:41.763
No.

821
38:42.656 --> 38:45.824
They say you shouldn't even speak to someone who hasn't read it.

822
38:45.824 --> 38:48.871
But I'm merciful, so I'll continue our conversation.

823
38:48.871 --> 38:51.329
- Do we push through, sir? - Anyway, just as the dead Zhuge Liang

824
38:51.329 --> 38:53.167
- Hold on. - drove off the living Sima Yi,

825
38:53.167 --> 38:56.417
the dead opposing force will defeat the living Special Forces.

826
38:56.417 --> 38:58.461
We're not dead yet.

827
38:58.461 --> 39:01.000
No. I'm making an analogy.

828
39:01.000 --> 39:02.215
I can't tell.

829
39:02.215 --> 39:04.959
They're acting so relaxed out in the open, it's definitely a trap.

830
39:04.959 --> 39:07.095
And that guy covering his ears

831
39:07.095 --> 39:09.334
must be talking on the radio through an earpiece.

832
39:09.334 --> 39:11.007
What do we do?

833
39:11.634 --> 39:13.643
Sergeant First Class Park, go around first. Just you.

834
39:13.643 --> 39:14.644
Understood.

835
39:14.644 --> 39:17.272
Our plan is like Zhuge Liang's,

836
39:17.272 --> 39:20.143
so I was drawing an analogy.

837
39:21.459 --> 39:23.602
- And you're just covering your ears. - Keep it down.

838
39:27.574 --> 39:29.375
- Are they gone? - Yes.

839
39:29.375 --> 39:31.911
What did I tell you? Didn't I say this would work?

840
39:31.911 --> 39:34.813
Now it really begins.

841
39:36.876 --> 39:39.241
[On Hill 200]

842
39:44.173 --> 39:46.259
Na Ri, the rice came out great today, right?

843
39:46.259 --> 39:49.125
I think it's the best rice we've ever made.

844
39:49.125 --> 39:53.141
I hope the Special Forces guys enjoy the food.

845
39:53.141 --> 39:55.292
I think this will be their best meal ever.

846
39:55.292 --> 39:56.888
Halt!

847
40:01.459 --> 40:02.584
Who are you?

848
40:02.584 --> 40:07.155
We're delivering meals to Special Forces.

849
40:07.155 --> 40:09.115
I'll go over today's menu.

850
40:09.115 --> 40:10.786
Spicy stir-fried pork, squid and radish soup,

851
40:10.786 --> 40:12.035
seasoned seaweed, kimchi,

852
40:12.035 --> 40:13.745
- and seasoned bean sprouts. - Hey,

853
40:13.745 --> 40:15.663
- don't overdo it. - Understood.

854
40:15.663 --> 40:17.290
Oh, you're cooks?

855
40:17.290 --> 40:18.709
- Yes. - Yes.

856
40:18.709 --> 40:20.176
Hold on.

857
40:28.468 --> 40:31.209
Something's off about this guy.

858
40:31.209 --> 40:34.557
Today's pork was too salty, so I added water and rice to balance it out,

859
40:34.557 --> 40:37.093
and now it's kind of...

860
40:39.584 --> 40:40.984
What?

861
40:41.981 --> 40:43.232
We're the opposing force.

862
40:43.232 --> 40:45.667
Oh, come on.

863
40:45.667 --> 40:47.904
We'll leave the food here.

864
40:47.904 --> 40:49.822
Take care.

865
40:49.822 --> 40:51.643
Enjoy your meal.

866
40:53.417 --> 40:55.840
Oh, come on.

867
40:58.998 --> 41:02.126
What a bunch of clowns.

868
41:02.126 --> 41:05.500
[On Hill 150]

869
41:05.500 --> 41:07.626
You idiots, finish this already!

870
41:07.626 --> 41:10.161
Dead men run laps in full gear later.

871
41:11.584 --> 41:14.347
Hey, I hear Sergeant First Class Park got killed.

872
41:14.347 --> 41:16.307
Jang Tae San's ranting over the radio.

873
41:16.307 --> 41:17.725
How is that possible?

874
41:17.725 --> 41:20.294
They're not even from the Scorpion Unit.

875
41:24.792 --> 41:27.110
Man down!

876
41:27.110 --> 41:30.178
Is anyone there? Please help us!

877
41:31.074 --> 41:32.949
Man down!

878
41:32.949 --> 41:35.792
Please help! Is anyone there?

879
41:35.792 --> 41:36.984
Do we fire?

880
41:36.984 --> 41:37.996
Wait.

881
41:37.996 --> 41:39.876
Something's wrong.

882
41:39.876 --> 41:41.960
- Move in. - Man down!

883
41:41.960 --> 41:44.651
Please help! Is anyone there?

884
41:48.792 --> 41:50.125
Don't shoot.

885
41:50.125 --> 41:51.834
He's hurt. Please help us.

886
41:51.834 --> 41:53.803
What happened?

887
41:53.803 --> 41:56.788
We were crawling, and I think he cut himself on something.

888
41:58.000 --> 42:00.250
He's bleeding badly.

889
42:00.250 --> 42:01.644
What do we do?

890
42:01.644 --> 42:03.646
We treat him first.

891
42:03.646 --> 42:06.858
- Put your weapons down and get over here. - Understood.

892
42:06.858 --> 42:09.384
- Staff Sergeant Kim, get a tourniquet. - Yes.

893
42:16.042 --> 42:17.329
Breathe. Keep breathing.

894
42:17.329 --> 42:18.411
Hang in there.

895
42:18.411 --> 42:19.620
Breathe.

896
42:19.620 --> 42:22.709
Sergeant Kang, hang in there a little longer.

897
42:22.709 --> 42:24.374
Hang in there.

898
42:25.376 --> 42:27.295
- It hurts! - Stay still.

899
42:27.295 --> 42:29.362
Do you want to bleed to death?

900
42:33.167 --> 42:35.250
The bleeding's under control.

901
42:35.250 --> 42:37.123
Let's close the wound.

902
42:40.125 --> 42:42.018
I haven't used this in a while, so it's a little stiff.

903
42:42.018 --> 42:43.945
Will it work?

904
42:50.068 --> 42:53.250
[Three minutes earlier]

905
42:53.250 --> 42:54.942
Now.

906
42:56.918 --> 42:59.118
Man down!

907
42:59.118 --> 43:02.187
Is anyone there? Please help us!

908
43:02.834 --> 43:05.292
Okay. Works fine.

909
43:05.292 --> 43:08.235
- Hold him down! - Yes.

910
43:09.042 --> 43:10.667
Hold still.

911
43:10.667 --> 43:13.000
Hang in there a little longer.

912
43:13.000 --> 43:14.379
Huh?

913
43:18.709 --> 43:21.432
Why does this blood smell nutty?

914
43:21.432 --> 43:23.061
- What? - What?

915
43:24.667 --> 43:25.853
Matdasi?

916
43:25.853 --> 43:27.271
You mean Matdasi?

917
43:27.271 --> 43:28.481
Would you like some rice?

918
43:28.481 --> 43:29.883
What? Rice?

919
43:35.083 --> 43:37.326
Let go!

920
43:38.417 --> 43:40.326
Let go!

921
43:42.453 --> 43:45.635
[Status: Dead]

922
43:51.667 --> 43:53.125
We really fell for that, huh?

923
43:53.125 --> 43:54.715
We really let our guard down.

924
43:54.715 --> 43:56.843
Still, how could we leave him when he said he was hurt?

925
43:56.843 --> 43:57.844
I'm sorry.

926
43:57.844 --> 44:00.390
You're good men. I'm sorry about this.

927
44:00.390 --> 44:01.767
Forget it.

928
44:01.767 --> 44:03.083
Good work, guys.

929
44:03.083 --> 44:05.393
- Let's go. - Thank you.

930
44:05.393 --> 44:07.751
Thank you. Chungseong!

931
44:07.751 --> 44:09.230
Pilseung!

932
44:09.230 --> 44:10.792
- Yeah. - Yeah.

933
44:10.792 --> 44:13.918
What do we do? We're going to get chewed out.

934
44:13.918 --> 44:15.250
This is Exercise Control.

935
44:15.250 --> 44:17.989
Attention all exercise controllers and participating units.

936
44:17.989 --> 44:21.834
All enemy Special Forces personnel have now been declared killed.

937
44:21.834 --> 44:24.334
I repeat. All Special Forces personnel have been killed.

938
44:24.334 --> 44:27.623
This officially concludes the opposing force exercise.

939
44:27.623 --> 44:31.088
All personnel, account for your spent casings and equipment at your current location.

940
44:31.088 --> 44:33.292
Then return to the designated assembly area.

941
44:33.292 --> 44:34.500
Out.

942
44:34.500 --> 44:36.834
Good work, First Lieutenant Oh.

943
44:36.834 --> 44:38.134
First Lieutenant Oh Kang Cheol.

944
44:38.134 --> 44:40.294
Thank you for all your hard work.

945
44:40.294 --> 44:42.506
- Thank you. - Yeah.

946
44:43.542 --> 44:44.560
Captain Cho?

947
44:44.560 --> 44:45.964
Yes.

948
44:48.352 --> 44:53.316
Don't you realize winning like this does nothing to develop their combat instincts?

949
44:53.316 --> 44:55.443
Isn't that what you told us yesterday?

950
44:55.443 --> 44:59.614
Shake things up and catch them off guard with dirty, underhanded tricks.

951
44:59.614 --> 45:01.908
I only did what you said.

952
45:01.908 --> 45:03.599
You taught me well.

953
45:08.205 --> 45:10.991
Guys, let's go home!

954
45:17.209 --> 45:20.885
Chungseong. This is Jang Tae San, the exercise controller.

955
45:20.885 --> 45:22.970
Yes, the exercise just ended.

956
45:22.970 --> 45:25.083
All Special Forces personnel were killed.

957
45:25.083 --> 45:26.766
- Park Cheol Yong! - Park Cheol Yong!

958
45:26.766 --> 45:29.185
- But Captain Cho Baek Ho... - Kang Mu Jeok!

959
45:29.185 --> 45:31.771
- Kang Mu Jeok! - Cho Baek Ho!

960
45:31.771 --> 45:33.314
- Choi Uk! - Choi Uk!

961
45:33.314 --> 45:36.934
He's tougher and more capable than I expected.

962
45:42.615 --> 45:46.035
That idiot Jang Tae San!

963
45:46.035 --> 45:48.167
I made a noncommissioned officer the exercise controller,

964
45:48.167 --> 45:50.456
and he got Special Forces wiped out?

965
45:50.456 --> 45:52.333
Cho Baek Ho got lucky.

966
45:52.333 --> 45:55.544
Now that jerk Cho Baek Ho will get all smug, too.

967
45:55.544 --> 45:59.298
Just thinking about it makes my blood pressure shoot up.

968
45:59.298 --> 46:03.302
He and Byeon Hyeok Jin already drive me up the wall.

969
46:03.302 --> 46:05.947
[Defense News Reporter Yoon]

970
46:06.764 --> 46:09.058
- Hello. - Hello, sir.

971
46:09.058 --> 46:10.393
This is Yoon from Defense News.

972
46:10.393 --> 46:12.812
Oh, Mr. Yoon. What can I do for you?

973
46:12.812 --> 46:17.108
I heard the opposing force drawn from an infantry division

974
46:17.108 --> 46:20.322
wiped out Special Forces in the Hoguk exercise.

975
46:20.322 --> 46:23.447
I'm told this is the first time in Army history

976
46:23.447 --> 46:28.452
that regular infantry has won so decisively as the opposing force.

977
46:28.452 --> 46:33.124
I heard you strongly recommended these soldiers for that role.

978
46:33.124 --> 46:36.610
Could I interview you about it?

979
46:38.626 --> 46:42.042
Oh, I hardly did anything.

980
46:42.042 --> 46:45.636
I've always emphasized realistic combat training.

981
46:45.636 --> 46:50.308
The men of Second Company, Seventh Battalion took that to heart more than anyone.

982
46:50.308 --> 46:54.002
So I strongly recommended them.

983
46:55.896 --> 46:58.649
What? I have to do my part.

984
46:58.649 --> 47:00.112
Yes, Mr. Yoon.

985
47:00.112 --> 47:01.777
Go ahead.

986
47:01.777 --> 47:04.947
Or why don't you just come over here?

987
47:04.947 --> 47:06.699
Yes.

988
47:06.699 --> 47:10.685
Then I'll get everything ready.

989
47:12.542 --> 47:13.706
Come on.

990
47:13.706 --> 47:15.584
It's about time I made general, too.

991
47:15.584 --> 47:17.584
Yes, of course.

992
47:17.584 --> 47:20.542
Who knew it'd turn out like this, huh?

993
47:21.300 --> 47:23.132
So much for that.

994
47:23.132 --> 47:24.633
- Good work. - You too.

995
47:24.633 --> 47:26.526
Thanks for everything.

996
47:28.000 --> 47:30.058
Thanks for all your hard work.

997
47:30.058 --> 47:33.225
Seriously, let's take leave together and go clubbing.

998
47:33.225 --> 47:35.895
If I visit Pohang, we're really going out to pick up women.

999
47:35.895 --> 47:37.900
- Seriously, come visit. - I really will.

1000
47:37.900 --> 47:40.566
We'll be the combat team, and you guys can be the operations team.

1001
47:40.566 --> 47:42.234
Seok Jin, we've got the looks.

1002
47:42.234 --> 47:44.070
We'll bring the looks, and they can bring the laughs.

1003
47:44.070 --> 47:45.792
Don't you have that backward?

1004
47:45.792 --> 47:47.876
Company Commander, which team has the looks?

1005
47:47.876 --> 47:50.128
You all look like bums to me.

1006
47:51.035 --> 47:54.455
Honestly, I looked down on you a little because you're in the Army.

1007
47:54.455 --> 47:57.124
But seeing how tough you are, I think I was wrong.

1008
47:57.124 --> 47:58.584
Thanks.

1009
47:58.584 --> 48:02.463
I wondered what was so special about those red name tags, too.

1010
48:02.463 --> 48:04.882
But after training with you, I'm impressed.

1011
48:04.882 --> 48:06.842
I had fun, even working this hard near discharge.

1012
48:06.842 --> 48:09.053
Stay healthy until you get out, too.

1013
48:09.053 --> 48:11.879
Thanks for everything.

1014
48:14.141 --> 48:16.452
Pilseung!

1015
48:17.728 --> 48:20.064
Chungseong!

1016
48:20.064 --> 48:21.717
Love you!

1017
48:22.483 --> 48:24.917
"Love you" is a bit much.

1018
48:26.821 --> 48:28.033
Thanks again.

1019
48:28.033 --> 48:30.452
- Good work. - Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

1020
48:30.452 --> 48:31.534
What's this?

1021
48:31.534 --> 48:34.036
You Army guys liked the semi-dried squid from Guryongpo,

1022
48:34.036 --> 48:35.913
so I packed some for you.

1023
48:35.913 --> 48:39.667
There's also a gift from the Marines, with our best wishes.

1024
48:39.667 --> 48:42.211
Please open it once you're back at your unit.

1025
48:42.211 --> 48:43.546
I'm touched.

1026
48:43.546 --> 48:44.709
Kim Sang Hun.

1027
48:44.709 --> 48:46.237
Yes.

1028
48:47.133 --> 48:49.318
- Here you go. - Oh, you don't have to.

1029
48:49.318 --> 48:52.140
Come on. It's a gift from all of us in the Army.

1030
48:52.140 --> 48:54.125
Please, take it.

1031
48:55.349 --> 48:57.196
Thanks for everything.

1032
49:00.187 --> 49:02.334
Oh, Matdasi.

1033
49:02.334 --> 49:04.918
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1034
49:04.918 --> 49:07.507
- You like it that much? - I do.

1035
49:09.334 --> 49:11.752
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

1036
49:12.491 --> 49:16.954
Thank you for everything, from the My Gummy candy to the Matdasi.

1037
49:16.954 --> 49:19.999
If you visit Jukdo Market in Pohang after discharge,

1038
49:19.999 --> 49:22.754
I'll buy you a plate of sashimi.

1039
49:22.754 --> 49:23.876
Really?

1040
49:23.876 --> 49:25.212
Can I really come?

1041
49:25.212 --> 49:26.375
Yes, please do!

1042
49:26.375 --> 49:30.301
My leave's coming up, so I'll come see you in Pohang.

1043
49:30.301 --> 49:32.636
When exactly are you coming?

1044
49:32.636 --> 49:36.515
Why are you so flustered? I'm kidding.

1045
49:36.515 --> 49:38.767
Thanks for everything.

1046
49:38.767 --> 49:41.312
I hope you stay healthy through the rest of your service.

1047
49:41.312 --> 49:45.382
I'll be sure to message you when I go to the computer room.

1048
49:46.167 --> 49:49.181
You promise?

1049
49:50.279 --> 49:52.459
Pilseung!

1050
49:52.459 --> 49:54.870
Chungseong! Love you!

1051
49:54.870 --> 49:56.500
Love you!

1052
49:58.334 --> 50:02.875
Just yesterday, you were at each other's throats.

1053
50:02.875 --> 50:05.211
Now you're one big family, huh?

1054
50:05.211 --> 50:08.881
- Yes! - I told you, no shouting.

1055
50:08.881 --> 50:14.860
Today, you were the best opposing force and a perfect team.

1056
50:14.860 --> 50:19.225
You'll be talking about today over drinks for the rest of your lives.

1057
50:19.225 --> 50:22.019
Head back to your units and finish your service strong.

1058
50:22.019 --> 50:23.938
- Understood? - Yes, sir!

1059
50:23.938 --> 50:25.000
Well done, everyone.

1060
50:25.000 --> 50:27.424
- Thank you, sir! - Thank you, sir!

1061
50:28.584 --> 50:30.110
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

1062
50:30.110 --> 50:31.779
Sergeant First Class Ma Tae Ho.

1063
50:31.779 --> 50:33.459
First Lieutenant Oh Kang Cheol.

1064
50:33.459 --> 50:34.964
Don't bother.

1065
50:36.751 --> 50:38.519
Stay healthy.

1066
50:41.375 --> 50:44.792
Everyone, attention!

1067
50:44.792 --> 50:48.048
Salute Master Sergeant Lee Jung Gu!

1068
50:48.048 --> 50:49.880
- Pilseung! - Pilseung!

1069
50:49.880 --> 50:51.632
Pilseung!

1070
50:51.632 --> 50:54.430
Pilseung!

1071
50:55.626 --> 50:57.034
Order arms!

1072
50:58.250 --> 51:00.832
- Thank you for all your hard work. - Thank you, too.

1073
51:08.334 --> 51:12.542
We wear different uniforms,

1074
51:12.542 --> 51:16.493
but we share the same mission

1075
51:16.493 --> 51:19.201
and resolve to defend our country.

1076
51:19.201 --> 51:21.811
I'm truly proud of you all.

1077
51:23.789 --> 51:28.627
Like a lion unfazed by noise.

1078
51:28.627 --> 51:33.385
Like the wind that no net can catch.

1079
51:33.385 --> 51:39.555
Like a lotus unstained by mud.

1080
51:39.555 --> 51:44.876
Let us walk alone, like the horn of a rhinoceros!

1081
51:44.876 --> 51:46.926
- Yes! - Yes!

1082
51:48.626 --> 51:49.876
Well done!

1083
51:49.876 --> 51:52.593
- Thank you, sir! - Thank you, sir!

1084
51:54.876 --> 51:58.202
Everyone, prepare to board!

1085
51:58.202 --> 52:02.042
[3:30 PM, Hoguk exercise ends] Single file! Forward, march!

1086
52:02.042 --> 52:03.579
- Bye! - Bye!

1087
52:03.579 --> 52:05.959
Thank you for everything.

1088
52:05.959 --> 52:07.808
Bye!

1089
52:15.500 --> 52:16.717
That shower felt good.

1090
52:16.717 --> 52:18.510
What's taking those guys so long?

1091
52:18.510 --> 52:20.974
- Hurry up, you guys! - We're all here.

1092
52:20.974 --> 52:25.291
All right, let's open the Marines' gift.

1093
52:30.584 --> 52:32.323
Open it up already.

1094
52:36.792 --> 52:38.209
Is red the only color they know?

1095
52:38.209 --> 52:40.209
Everything's red.

1096
52:40.209 --> 52:41.734
Let's see...

1097
52:42.368 --> 52:43.459
Oh, this is...

1098
52:43.459 --> 52:44.540
This is...

1099
52:44.540 --> 52:46.901
- Semi-dried squid! - Semi-dried squid!

1100
52:48.666 --> 52:49.833
- Nice. - Thank you.

1101
52:49.833 --> 52:51.752
- That's a lot. - There's more here.

1102
52:51.752 --> 52:52.959
Thank you.

1103
52:52.959 --> 52:54.083
Huh?

1104
52:54.083 --> 52:55.918
What's this?

1105
52:55.918 --> 52:57.523
A letter?

1106
53:00.472 --> 53:02.471
What is this?

1107
53:02.471 --> 53:07.101
Doesn't it look like some kind of hex written in blood?

1108
53:07.101 --> 53:09.687
Looks like writing.

1109
53:09.687 --> 53:12.751
- Let me try reading it. - Oh, Hanguk University.

1110
53:12.751 --> 53:14.987
Wait, Moon Bit Na Ri. You can read that?

1111
53:14.987 --> 53:18.654
My dad was a Marine. I can make some of it out.

1112
53:18.654 --> 53:20.147
Really?

1113
53:25.994 --> 53:27.918
I think it says something nice.

1114
53:27.918 --> 53:29.918
Oh, come on.

1115
53:29.918 --> 53:33.335
It's the thought that counts, right?

1116
53:33.335 --> 53:35.045
Bit Na Ri, keep that safe in your locker.

1117
53:35.045 --> 53:36.876
Yes!

1118
53:36.876 --> 53:38.927
- I'll do it right. - You scared me.

1119
53:38.927 --> 53:41.954
All right, grab your semi-dried squid. Dismissed!

1120
53:42.806 --> 53:44.263
Let's go.

1121
53:44.263 --> 53:46.167
- Thank you. - Hurry up and unpack your gear.

1122
53:46.167 --> 53:47.876
- Will do. - Good work.

1123
53:47.876 --> 53:50.066
- Good work. - Good work.

1124
53:50.066 --> 53:52.232
Huh? What's this?

1125
53:52.232 --> 53:53.689
- What's that? - What's that?

1126
53:53.689 --> 53:56.987
- Oh, man. - You can't just steal these!

1127
53:56.987 --> 53:59.528
- What do you mean, steal? Are you nuts? - You didn't?

1128
53:59.528 --> 54:02.283
Hey, if he didn't steal them...

1129
54:04.036 --> 54:05.743
Looks like they're gifts.

1130
54:05.743 --> 54:07.327
- Awesome. - Really?

1131
54:07.327 --> 54:10.164
- Kim Sang Hun. - Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

1132
54:10.164 --> 54:13.250
- Park Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok.

1133
54:13.250 --> 54:15.584
[Corporal Park Min Seok] Oh, my name's on it!

1134
54:15.584 --> 54:18.091
I really wanted one of these.

1135
54:18.091 --> 54:22.926
They look tough, but they've got a cute side, huh?

1136
54:22.926 --> 54:24.723
Grab yours.

1137
54:24.723 --> 54:25.933
Awesome.

1138
54:25.933 --> 54:27.556
What size is this?

1139
54:27.556 --> 54:29.850
- How'd they know our sizes? - There are shorts, too.

1140
54:29.850 --> 54:32.102
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun and Corporal Kim Dong Woo,

1141
54:32.102 --> 54:34.062
Marine red really suits you.

1142
54:34.062 --> 54:36.482
- You think? - They look good on you.

1143
54:36.482 --> 54:39.146
- Pilseung! - Pilseung!

1144
54:41.445 --> 54:45.515
We should've given them T-shirts or something, too.

1145
54:46.578 --> 54:48.542
You look cool.

1146
54:48.542 --> 54:51.187
They've got a sentimental side, huh?

1147
54:52.873 --> 54:55.060
To our Army comrades.

1148
54:55.959 --> 54:58.879
Though our name tags differ in color,

1149
54:58.879 --> 55:00.672
Sergeant Kang.

1150
55:00.672 --> 55:02.216
- Marines! - Are you kidding me?

1151
55:02.216 --> 55:03.292
Just have it.

1152
55:03.292 --> 55:06.345
we felt each other's warmth, back to back on the blood-soaked battlefield.

1153
55:06.345 --> 55:07.346
We can do it.

1154
55:07.346 --> 55:08.876
Our time together was short,

1155
55:08.876 --> 55:13.352
but we'll remember your courage forever.

1156
55:13.352 --> 55:16.292
Best of luck with the rest of your service.

1157
55:16.292 --> 55:19.000
From all of us in the Marine Amphibious Raiding Battalion.

1158
55:19.000 --> 55:21.665
Pilseung!

1159
55:22.876 --> 55:24.243
P.S.

1160
55:24.867 --> 55:27.588
We'll enjoy the Matdasi.

1161
55:55.769 --> 55:57.537
[Practice Communications Security]

1162
56:02.651 --> 56:04.403
Communication security. Corporal Sung Yoon Mo speaking.

1163
56:04.403 --> 56:06.125
How can I help you?

1164
56:06.125 --> 56:07.558
Well...

1165
56:10.701 --> 56:11.792
Hello?

1166
56:11.792 --> 56:13.745
Say "Communication security," not "Hello."

1167
56:13.745 --> 56:16.751
Oh, communication security. How can I help you?

1168
56:16.751 --> 56:20.459
I haven't been sleeping well lately.

1169
56:20.459 --> 56:21.837
Sorry?

1170
56:21.837 --> 56:24.093
I can't eat much, either.

1171
56:24.801 --> 56:25.876
Oh, geez.

1172
56:25.876 --> 56:28.844
A senior soldier keeps picking on me.

1173
56:28.844 --> 56:32.793
I don't know who to talk to about it.

1174
56:34.474 --> 56:37.561
Why don't you talk to your squad leader?

1175
56:37.561 --> 56:39.274
That's a bit tricky.

1176
56:39.274 --> 56:40.776
What about your company commander?

1177
56:40.776 --> 56:43.737
I'm afraid that'll only make things worse.

1178
56:43.737 --> 56:45.625
Then someone you enlisted with?

1179
56:46.281 --> 56:47.905
What is it? Who's that?

1180
56:47.905 --> 56:50.369
I think it's a soldier who's struggling with military life.

1181
56:50.369 --> 56:52.320
Why are you handling that?

1182
56:52.320 --> 56:54.918
- Sorry? - There's nothing we can do.

1183
56:54.918 --> 56:58.248
Just give him the Defense Helpline number.

1184
57:00.292 --> 57:04.004
Communication security. Here's what you can do.

1185
57:04.004 --> 57:06.298
Don't suffer in silence.

1186
57:06.298 --> 57:09.051
Call the Defense Helpline.

1187
57:09.051 --> 57:10.969
The Defense Helpline?

1188
57:10.969 --> 57:13.038
What's the number?

1189
57:13.809 --> 57:15.729
The number...

1190
57:17.729 --> 57:19.089
It's 1303.

1191
57:19.089 --> 57:21.146
That's right.

1192
57:21.146 --> 57:24.566
If you're facing verbal abuse, assault, or human rights violations in your unit,

1193
57:24.566 --> 57:27.083
call 1303.

1194
57:27.083 --> 57:32.240
The Defense Helpline is open 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.

1195
57:32.240 --> 57:34.083
Understood. Thank you.

1196
57:34.083 --> 57:36.253
I'll call right now.

1197
57:38.997 --> 57:40.165
You're getting better.

1198
57:40.165 --> 57:41.875
I'm pretty good now, right?

1199
57:41.875 --> 57:43.125
I'm a pro.

1200
57:43.125 --> 57:44.795
Well, then get back to work.

1201
57:44.795 --> 57:46.667
Could I have one, too?

1202
57:46.667 --> 57:48.215
Eat your own.

1203
57:48.215 --> 57:49.633
I don't have any.

1204
57:49.633 --> 57:51.500
- And if you do? - I have some.

1205
57:51.500 --> 57:53.626
You lied. Hold out your hand.

1206
57:53.626 --> 57:56.205
I'll call 1303.

1207
57:59.083 --> 58:00.751
I'm sorry.

1208
58:00.751 --> 58:02.396
I'm sorry.

1209
58:02.396 --> 58:04.212
I'm sorry.

1210
58:12.167 --> 58:13.573
The Defense Helpline.

1211
58:13.573 --> 58:15.267
1303.
